WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:02.910
- [Narrator] Floating on
the Mediterranean Sea,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.380
this castle protected an ancient port city

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.140
for hundreds of years.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.740
It's also a place shrouded in myth

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.576
where a legendary princess
met a certain fate.

00:00:12.576 --> 00:00:15.159
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.000
Just about 700 feet off the
coast of Southern Turkey,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.550
the Kizkalesi, or maiden's castle,

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.720
sits on an island so tiny it looks

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.143
like it's standing on water.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.450
The walls and towers
of the castle date back

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.490
to the early 12th century,

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.693
although exactly who
built it is a mystery.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.780
According to one legend, a Byzantine king

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.170
built the castle after a
fortune teller told him

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.720
that his only daughter
would die from a snake bite.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.060
Despite the king's efforts
to protect the princess,

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.730
a snake snuck in by
hiding in a fruit basket

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.973
and the princess met her unfortunate fate.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.500
Fortified walls wrap
around the entire complex

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.110
with eight towers
providing 360-degree views,

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.210
making the castle an effective first line

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.133
of defense against enemy
ships approaching the port.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.760
The legend of the 12th century may be

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.960
a thing of the past, but the stone walls

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.683
of the fortress still stand
today, keeping their secrets.

00:01:20.026 --> 00:01:22.526
(chime dings)

